v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-207_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"8309b909-b742-470c-83a4-e3c51bc85e4a","comments":[],"created_at":1783968886550627001,"creation_channel":"unknown","deps":[],"description":"## Local dev / agent clone identity setup + docs\n\nEach human/agent clone writes non-exempt tickets and needs its OWN identity (not the bot).\n\n- Document the setup in `docs/identity.md` / `docs/local-dev-env.md`: create/own an identity ticket, `rebar identity use <id>` (writes git-ignored `.rebar/current_identity`), and set `identity.signing_key` (or export `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY`) to the developer's local SSH private key under `~/.ssh/`.\n- Note the `git config user.email` fallback resolution path.\n- Make explicit that the signing key is per-machine and never committed.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/identity.md` (and/or `docs/local-dev-env.md`) documents the per-clone identity + signing-key setup and the git-email fallback.\n- [ ] A local clone following the docs produces a signed write, verifiable via `rebar show <id>` (the written event shows `authorship.signed ≥ 1`) and/or `rebar verify-authorship` emitting a `verified` verdict for it. (NOT `verify-signature`, which certifies HMAC manifest attestations from the `rebar sign` flow, not SSH-based event authorship.)\n- [ ] Docs state the key is per-machine and uncommitted.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","297d-a233-ce1b-4484"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"","parent_status_uuid":"3f020b04-34c6-40a5-969e-58b059b64510","plan_review_phase":"execution","precondition